# built model files - regenerable in minutes by ocrcer-build, never committed
*.ocrw
model/build/

# rendered glyph sheets and intermediate feature dumps
model/cache/

# rust
target/

# benchmark outputs
fixtures/results/

# the generated comparison corpus: hundreds of MB of pages that
# `ocrcer-build pages` reproduces byte for byte from the authored text in
# `crates/ocrcer-build/src/corpus.rs`. The text is committed; the pixels are
# not. Distinct from `fixtures/pages`, which holds the small blessed set
# ARCHITECTURE.md section 8.2 describes and which IS committed.
bench/pages/
# the held-out corpus: same generator, render sizes deliberately absent
# from both `bench/pages/` and every prototype-bank scale, so a bank
# composition chosen on `bench/pages/` can be checked against sizes it
# was not chosen on.
bench/holdout/
# a diagnostic corpus: every integer render size across a range, to look at
# accuracy as a curve in resolution rather than at five points.
bench/sizesweep/
bench/sizesweep-hi/
# the same four corpora re-rendered with coverage, which is what every figure
# dated after ARCHITECTURE.md section 11's truth-box entry is measured on. The
# two-valued originals are kept beside them only for that entry's side by side
# and are not what anything should be measured against.
bench/pages-cov/
bench/holdout-cov/
bench/sizesweep-cov/
bench/sizesweep-hi-cov/

# Third-party evaluation material downloaded from the web: real accounting
# documents in the many shapes real clients send. It lives OUTSIDE this
# repository, at D:/Dev/ExcludedPrivate/ocrcer/, and the rule is that it is
# evaluation *input* and never model *content* - see ARCHITECTURE.md section
# 11's corpus-provenance entry. These two patterns exist only so that a
# stray copy made inside the working tree cannot be committed by accident.
bench/private/
bench/*-private/
bench/priv*/
# and the same for a corpus built from a downloaded dataset, which is third-
# party material under the identical rule.
bench/datasets/
bench/scribe/
bench/finfilings/
